Implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the booklesss project

SUMMARY:
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects.

CHANGES MADE:

1. Installed Dependencies:
   - Added @vercel/speed-insights package to project dependencies
   - Updated package.json and package-lock.json accordingly

2. Modified Files:
   - src/app/layout.tsx: Added SpeedInsights integration to the root layout

IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS:

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I implemented the integration for Next.js v13.5+ using the App Router pattern:

- Imported `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Added the `<SpeedInsights />` component to the body of the root layout
- Positioned it alongside other monitoring components (RegisterSW, DesktopGate)

The component was placed at the end of the body, following the existing pattern of mounting utility components at the root level. This ensures Speed Insights will track performance metrics across all routes in the application.

VERIFICATION:

✓ Build completed successfully (278 static pages generated)
✓ No TypeScript errors introduced
✓ ESLint shows no new errors in modified files
✓ Lock files updated to reflect new dependency

NEXT STEPS:

To activate Speed Insights:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. Performance data will begin collecting automatically after deployment
4. Access metrics through the Vercel Speed Insights dashboard

The implementation follows Next.js App Router best practices and integrates seamlessly with the existing project architecture.
